/28 "I don't have one of those."
/29 "I'm already wearing the _."
/30 "Y"
/31 "N"
/32 "More..."
/33 ">"
/34 " "
/35 " "
/36 "I now have the _."
/37 "I'm now wearing the _."
/38 "I've removed the _."
/39 "I've dropped the _."
/40 "I can't wear the _."
/41 "I can't remove the _."
/42 "I can't remove the _. My hands are full."
/43 "The _ weighs too much for me."
/44 "The _ is in the"
/45 "The _ isn't in the"
/46 ", "
/47 " and "
/48 ".#n"
/49 "I don't have the _."
/50 "I'm not wearing the _."
/51 "."
/52 "There isn't one of those in the"
/53 "Nothing."
/54 " "
/55 " "
/56 " "
/57 "I/O Error"
/58 " "
/59 "File name error."
/60 "Type in name of file."
/MTX
/0 "NEXTDAAD - LAYER 2 TRANSPARENCY / PUNCH-OUT FIXTURE"
/OTX
/0 "a brass lamp"
/LTX
/0 ""
/1 ""
/CON
/0
NORTH 1
/1
SOUTH 0
/OBJ
/0    1   1   _ _  _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _   _ _
/PRO 0
; The driver. Location 0 is the "not painted yet" state: the first pass
; paints the ruler and brings the card up, then moves to location 1 so
; every later pass is just the toggle. eng_run re-enters PRO 0 whenever
; the process stack unwinds (src\engine.asm:187), so this IS the loop -
; there is no PARSE anywhere in this fixture and nothing ever prints a
; prompt over the ruler.
> _ _   AT 0
        PROCESS 1
        GOTO 1
        DONE
> _ _   ANYKEY
        PROCESS 4
        DONE
/PRO 1
; Screen build, in the only order that works: the full-screen window is
; sized and cleared BEFORE anything is printed into it, the ruler is
; printed top to bottom, and only then does the card go up - so a fault
; in the blit cannot be confused with a half-drawn ruler.
;
; MODE 2 disables the "More..." pager for window 0 (h_mode writes
; WIN_FLAGS, bit 1 = disable More - src\overlay0.asm:1563). Without it
; the pager fires after 31 printed lines, stops the fill dead and prints
; SM32 across the ruler.
> _ _   WINDOW 0
        WINAT 0 0
        WINSIZE 32 80
        MODE 2
        PAPER 1
        INK 15
        CLS
        PROCESS 2
        PROCESS 3
; The 1x1 parking window for every later ANYKEY - see the header.
> _ _   WINDOW 1
        WINAT 31 79
        WINSIZE 1 1
        MODE 2
        PAPER 1
        INK 15
> _ _   PICTURE 1
        DISPLAY 0
        DONE
> _ _   WINDOW 0
        CLS
        INK 10
        MES "***-PICTURE-1-F "
        MES "AILED-NO-001-NX "
        MES "I-STAGED-STOP-N "
        MES "OTHING-BELOW-IS "
        MES "-A-RESULT...... "
        DONE
/PRO 4
; The A/B toggle. Flag 100 remembers which state the screen is in.
; DISPLAY 1 clears the Layer 2 plane to the transparent index and flips
; (h_display's non-zero arm, src\overlay2.asm:924) so the WHOLE ruler
; shows; DISPLAY 0 re-blits the staged card. Nothing else changes - the
; tilemap is never reprinted, so any difference between the two states
; belongs to Layer 2 alone.
> _ _   ZERO fToggle
        DISPLAY 1
        SET fToggle
        DONE
> _ _   DISPLAY 0
        CLEAR fToggle
        DONE
/PRO 2
; Ruler rows 0..15. One entry per row, five INK + MES pairs per entry,
; each MES exactly 15 non-space characters plus the flushing space.
